KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ third element forwarded: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A variadic constructor whose trailing parameter pack has two or more elements
must expand to one parameter per element and expand the pack in the
member-initializer arguments.  The single-element case works by substitution,
but the multi-element case is not expanded, so construction of a three-element
TImpl silently fails and main is truncated.  Flip to CORE once multi-element
parameter-pack expansion is implemented.
